,"stem":234,"icon":235},"CRI Format","\u002Fplatform\u002Freference\u002Fcri-format","04.platform\u002F12.reference\u002F01.cri-format","i-lucide-link",{"title":237,"path":238,"stem":239,"icon":240},"Grind Jobs","\u002Fplatform\u002Freference\u002Fgrind-jobs","04.platform\u002F12.reference\u002F02.grind-jobs","i-lucide-workflow",{"title":242,"path":243,"stem":244,"icon":179},"Project Publishing Design","\u002Fplatform\u002Freference\u002Fproject-publishing-design","04.platform\u002F12.reference\u002F03.project-publishing-design",{"title":246,"path":247,"stem":248,"icon":38},"Sign-In Design","\u002Fplatform\u002Freference\u002Fsign-in-design","04.platform\u002F12.reference\u002F04.sign-in-design",{"title":250,"path":251,"stem":252,"icon":253},"Development Server","\u002Fplatform\u002Fdevelopment-server","04.platform\u002F13.development-server","i-lucide-server-cog",{"title":255,"path":256,"stem":257,"icon":258},"Supply Chain Security","\u002Fplatform\u002Fsupply-chain-security","04.platform\u002F14.supply-chain-security","i-lucide-package-check",{"title":260,"path":261,"stem":262,"icon":263},"Enterprise License","\u002Fplatform\u002Fenterprise-license","04.platform\u002F15.enterprise-license","i-lucide-badge-check",{"id":265,"title":232,"body":266,"description":1238,"extension":1239,"links":1240,"meta":1241,"navigation":1242,"path":233,"seo":1243,"stem":234,"__hash__":1244},"docs\u002F04.platform\u002F12.reference\u002F01.cri-format.md",{"type":267,"value":268,"toc":1221},"minimark",[269,273,277,281,292,299,303,313,319,323,328,331,370,374,381,388,394,398,405,460,466,476,489,553,556,624,627,631,634,640,644,647,653,657,660,666,670,677,917,921,927,1128,1132,1217],[270,271,31],"h2",{"id":272},"overview",[274,275,276],"p",{},"A CRI (Kinotic Resource Identifier) is used by Kinotic to route requests to the appropriate service, method, or event stream. It is a URI-like format with parts named for clarity within the Kinotic platform.",[270,278,280],{"id":279},"format","Format",[282,283,288],"pre",{"className":284,"code":286,"language":287},[285],"language-text","scheme:\u002F\u002F[scope@][zone~]resourceName[\u002Fpath][#version]\n","text",[289,290,286],"code",{"__ignoreMap":291},"",[274,293,294,295,298],{},"Everything in brackets (",[289,296,297],{},"[]",") is optional.",[270,300,302],{"id":301},"case","Case",[274,304,305,306,309,310,312],{},"Every part keeps the case it was written with, and addresses match by exact string comparison — ",[289,307,308],{},"OrderService"," and ",[289,311,308],{}," are two different addresses. Service names carry the case of the class that published them, so a typical address looks like:",[282,314,317],{"className":315,"code":316,"language":287},[285],"srv:\u002F\u002Fmanagement-api~org.kinotic.management.api.services.ProjectService\u002FfindByRepoFullName\n",[289,318,316],{"__ignoreMap":291},[270,320,322],{"id":321},"components","Components",[324,325,327],"h3",{"id":326},"scheme","Scheme",[274,329,330],{},"Identifies the type of resource being addressed.",[332,333,334,346],"table",{},[335,336,337],"thead",{},[338,339,340,343],"tr",{},[341,342,327],"th",{},[341,344,345],{},"Description",[347,348,349,360],"tbody",{},[338,350,351,357],{},[352,353,354],"td",{},[289,355,356],{},"srv",[352,358,359],{},"Published services and their methods",[338,361,362,367],{},[352,363,364],{},[289,365,366],{},"stream",[352,368,369],{},"Event streams (not yet routable through the gateway)",[324,371,373],{"id":372},"scope","Scope",[274,375,376,377,380],{},"An optional qualifier that narrows the CRI to a specific context, such as a tenant ID, user ID, or device ID. When present, it appears before the ",[289,378,379],{},"@"," symbol.",[274,382,383,384,387],{},"If a scope needs sub-scopes, use the format ",[289,385,386],{},"scope:sub-scope",".",[282,389,392],{"className":390,"code":391,"language":287},[285],"srv:\u002F\u002Ftenant-123@app.acme-org.orders-app~OrderService\nstream:\u002F\u002Fdevice-42@app.acme-org.orders-app~temperature\u002Fsensor-1\n",[289,393,391],{"__ignoreMap":291},[324,395,397],{"id":396},"zone","Zone",[274,399,400,401,404],{},"The optional zone places the resource in the isolation boundary the gateway validates on every send and subscribe. It precedes the resourceName, separated by ",[289,402,403],{},"~",". A zone is one or more dot-separated labels of lowercase letters, digits, and interior dashes.",[332,406,407,415],{},[335,408,409],{},[338,410,411,413],{},[341,412,397],{},[341,414,345],{},[347,416,417,430,440,450],{},[338,418,419,424],{},[352,420,421],{},[289,422,423],{},"app.\u003CorganizationId>.\u003CapplicationId>",[352,425,426,427,387],{},"One application's services. Only that application's participants and the owning organization's runtimes can call them, through the app server, the one server that reaches these zones; they are hosted by the owning organization's runtime, which authenticates as an organization participant. Applications may nest their own sub-zones, e.g. ",[289,428,429],{},"app.acme-org.orders-app.billing",[338,431,432,437],{},[352,433,434],{},[289,435,436],{},"app-api",[352,438,439],{},"The platform's data plane for applications, such as entity persistence and named query execution. Hosted in-process by the platform only.",[338,441,442,447],{},[352,443,444],{},[289,445,446],{},"management-api",[352,448,449],{},"The platform services organizations manage the system through, such as member, application, and entity definition management. Hosted in-process by the platform only.",[338,451,452,457],{},[352,453,454],{},[289,455,456],{},"system-api",[352,458,459],{},"The system's own services. Only system participants can call or host them.",[274,461,462,463,465],{},"A cluster member outside the platform's servers can host its services in ",[289,464,446],{},", where organizations' users call them through the management server as they call the platform's own; such a service checks the caller's organization itself.",[274,467,468,469,472,473,475],{},"Organization and application ids become zone labels, but only ever after the ",[289,470,471],{},"app"," prefix, so they cannot collide with the platform's own zones. The one exception is guarded explicitly: creating an organization or application whose name slugifies to ",[289,474,456],{}," is rejected.",[274,477,478,479,481,482,485,486,488],{},"Which zones a connection may address is determined by the authenticated participant. A participant may also address any sub-zone of a zone it is allowed, so ",[289,480,429],{}," is reachable by whoever may reach ",[289,483,484],{},"app.acme-org.orders-app",". An address without a ",[289,487,403],{}," carries no zone at all and is only reachable by system participants.",[332,490,491,504],{},[335,492,493],{},[338,494,495,498,501],{},[341,496,497],{},"Participant",[341,499,500],{},"May send to",[341,502,503],{},"May subscribe to",[347,505,506,522,541],{},[338,507,508,511,519],{},[352,509,510],{},"APPLICATION (org, app)",[352,512,513,515,516],{},[289,514,436],{},", ",[289,517,518],{},"app.\u003Corg>.\u003Capp>",[352,520,521],{},"reply destinations only",[338,523,524,527,536],{},[352,525,526],{},"ORGANIZATION (org)",[352,528,529,515,531,515,533],{},[289,530,446],{},[289,532,436],{},[289,534,535],{},"app.\u003Corg>.*",[352,537,538,540],{},[289,539,535],{}," — its applications' zones",[338,542,543,546,549],{},[352,544,545],{},"SYSTEM",[352,547,548],{},"everything",[352,550,551],{},[289,552,456],{},[274,554,555],{},"Each server also has a zone partitioning, the zones it hosts and the zones it reaches. A node advertises a service\nto the cluster only in a zone its server hosts, and sends only to zones its server reaches: an address in any\nother zone has no handlers there. An address without a zone passes both.",[332,557,558,571],{},[335,559,560],{},[338,561,562,565,568],{},[341,563,564],{},"Server",[341,566,567],{},"Hosts",[341,569,570],{},"Reaches",[347,572,573,590,607],{},[338,574,575,578,582],{},[352,576,577],{},"org",[352,579,580],{},[289,581,446],{},[352,583,584,515,586,515,588],{},[289,585,446],{},[289,587,456],{},[289,589,436],{},[338,591,592,595,601],{},[352,593,594],{},"system",[352,596,597,515,599],{},[289,598,456],{},[289,600,446],{},[352,602,603,515,605],{},[289,604,456],{},[289,606,446],{},[338,608,609,611,618],{},[352,610,471],{},[352,612,613,515,615],{},[289,614,436],{},[289,616,617],{},"app.*",[352,619,620,515,622],{},[289,621,436],{},[289,623,617],{},[274,625,626],{},"The gateway applies the partitioning before a frame reaches the event bus: a send to a zone the server does not\nreach, or a subscription in a zone it does not host, is refused whatever the participant may address. The\nservice directory and listener monitors still see every registration in the cluster, so a service hosted by one\nserver shows as online from any other, while each server's MCP listing shows only the tools in zones it reaches.",[324,628,630],{"id":629},"resource-name","Resource Name",[274,632,633],{},"The name of the resource being addressed, excluding the zone. For services, this is the fully qualified service name. For streams, this is the event type name.",[282,635,638],{"className":636,"code":637,"language":287},[285],"srv:\u002F\u002Fmanagement-api~com.example.UserService\nstream:\u002F\u002Fapp.acme-org.orders-app~temperature\n",[289,639,637],{"__ignoreMap":291},[324,641,643],{"id":642},"path","Path",[274,645,646],{},"An optional path that identifies a specific part of the resource, such as a method name on a service. The path's case is preserved.",[282,648,651],{"className":649,"code":650,"language":287},[285],"srv:\u002F\u002Fmanagement-api~com.example.UserService\u002FfindById\nstream:\u002F\u002Fapp.acme-org.orders-app~temperature\u002Fsensor-1\n",[289,652,650],{"__ignoreMap":291},[324,654,656],{"id":655},"version","Version",[274,658,659],{},"An optional semantic version for the resource. Enables versioned service routing so multiple versions of a service can coexist.",[282,661,664],{"class